-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-20T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Broomfield, CO; Douglas, CO; Denver, CO; Weld, CO; Boulder, CO; Jefferson, CO; Larimer, CO; Arapahoe, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.34156115e6b0d467e8b45dc0f7f2b946c514cada.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.34156115e6b0d467e8b45dc0f7f2b946c514cada.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-20T20:31:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 202031 CCA AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion...CORRECTED National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 231 PM MDT Thu Aug 20 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Isolated showers and storms in the mountains mainly south of I-70 ending this evening. - Hot Friday with high temperatures pushing 100F over portions of the plains and I-25 Corridor. High based late afternoon and evening showers/storm/virga","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-20T19:47:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Friday... Very warm temperatures today will warm even further to near record levels for Friday. Humidity recovery tonight will be good over the eastern plains and high mountain valleys, but only moderate at best in the foothills and thermal belts of the mountains. Under Friday's heat, minimum RH will drop into the 12-18% range over most areas, but 20-26% over th","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":null,"aviation":{"icao":"KGXY","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KGXY 202056Z 06007KT 10SM CLR 33/09 A3018 RMK AO2 SLP171 T03330089 57012","temp_f":92,"wind_dir":60